      "start_seconds": 1.36,
      "end_seconds": 5.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.16,
      "end_seconds": 11.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.09,
      "end_seconds": 19.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "well, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.75,
      "end_seconds": 24.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 26.15,
      "end_seconds": 32.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "He's been having itchy red patches that have gone crusty, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.14,
      "end_seconds": 36.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.42,
      "end_seconds": 43.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "about about a month, uh, give or take"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.56,
      "end_seconds": 48.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "It was closer to about two months, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.56,
      "end_seconds": 59.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "okay, so roughly one to two months is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.37,
      "end_seconds": 76.4,
      "duration_seconds": 12.03,
      "text": "That sounds about right. Yeah, there's being irritable as well. I've, I've had scratching at night too, for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.88,
      "end_seconds": 85.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Have you had itchy red patches that have gone crusty before, or is this the the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.11,
      "end_seconds": 94.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "a bit, about six months ago. It It settled by itself back then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.75,
      "end_seconds": 98.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "have you had any high fever, blisters or drowsiness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.14,
      "end_seconds": 105.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "I haven't had high fever, blisters or drowsiness, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.46,
      "end_seconds": 109.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "mm, okay have you had eating poorly, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.7,
      "end_seconds": 115.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No. No eating poorly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 121.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.3,
      "end_seconds": 125.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "no weakness or anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.45,
      "end_seconds": 134.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "So, anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.68,
      "end_seconds": 138.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "I've got eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.32,
      "end_seconds": 143.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Alright, eczema, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.05,
      "end_seconds": 155.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.62,
      "end_seconds": 168.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days. My husband and I live above the shop. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.01,
      "end_seconds": 183.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.53,
      "end_seconds": 186.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.42,
      "end_seconds": 192.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.81,
      "end_seconds": 196.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.64,
      "end_seconds": 201.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Alright, tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.13,
      "end_seconds": 211.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "I'm on hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema. A moisturiser, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.73,
      "end_seconds": 215.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "let me take your readings now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.38,
      "end_seconds": 227.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.52,
      "end_seconds": 247.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "okay: temperature 36.5, pulse 76, pressure 120 over 76, oxygen saturation is 99 percent"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.92,
      "end_seconds": 252.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.88,
      "end_seconds": 264.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.82,
      "end_seconds": 267.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "okay, nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.03,
      "end_seconds": 290.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "The eczema patches on the the arms have yellow crusts and weeping areas."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.54,
      "end_seconds": 293.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.99,
      "end_seconds": 326.23,
      "duration_seconds": 28.24,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Okay, thinking it through, it points towards eczema with a bacterial skin infection. I'll request a skin swab, it'll help with infected eczema. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. You'll be taking flucloxacillin, 250 milligrams, four times a day, seven days. It's for infected eczema. Keep the nails short and keep using the moisturiser."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.11,
      "end_seconds": 339.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Please come and see me in one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.39,
      "end_seconds": 342.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "yes, that's manageable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.8,
      "end_seconds": 347.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.12,
      "end_seconds": 350.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
